From: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pipewire: cast the registry proxy back to pw_registry

PipeWire 1.6 made pw_registry_add_listener a typed inline function taking a
struct pw_registry *. It used to be a macro that took the proxy, which is why
this file stores the registry as a struct pw_proxy * - it destroys it with
pw_proxy_destroy - and passes that same pointer here. With the typed
declaration the build stops:

  ../src/pipewire.c:332:35: error: passing argument 1 of
  'pw_registry_add_listener' from incompatible pointer type
  [-Wincompatible-pointer-types]
  note: expected 'struct pw_registry *' but argument is of type
  'struct pw_proxy *'

The pointer is a registry - four lines above it is the return value of
pw_core_get_registry, cast to pw_proxy * for storage - so cast it back at the
call site. That keeps pw_proxy_destroy correct on the field and leaves the
lifetime handling alone.

Signed-off-by: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>

--- a/src/pipewire.c
+++ b/src/pipewire.c
@@ -329,7 +329,7 @@
   remote->registry = (struct pw_proxy*) pw_core_get_registry (remote->core,
                                                               PW_VERSION_REGISTRY,
                                                               0);
-  pw_registry_add_listener (remote->registry,
+  pw_registry_add_listener ((struct pw_registry *) remote->registry,
                             &remote->registry_listener,
                             &registry_events,
                             remote);
